    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h3><a name="1.ProjectObjective"></a>1. Project Objective</h3>

<p><b>Sunil Store Grocery</b> is a mobile-friendly grocery ordering web application that allows customers to browse grocery products, search products by name or category, add products to a shopping cart, provide customer details, and place an order online.</p>

<p>After placing an order, the system generates a unique <b>Order ID</b>. The customer contacts the store by phone, and the store confirms the order before processing it.</p>

<p>The application will also provide an <b>Admin Panel</b> where authorized store staff can view and manage customer orders and product information.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="2.MainCustomerRequirement"></a>2. Main Customer Requirement</h1>

<h3><a name="CustomerUserStory"></a>Customer User Story</h3>

<p><b>As a customer, I want to browse grocery products, add products to my cart, provide my details, and place an order so that I can conveniently order groceries from Sunil Store.</b></p>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Customer can access the Home page.</li>
	<li>Customer can view available products.</li>
	<li>Customer can search for products.</li>
	<li>Customer can browse products by category.</li>
	<li>Customer can view product details.</li>
	<li>Customer can add products to the cart.</li>
	<li>Customer can update product quantity.</li>
	<li>Customer can remove products from the cart.</li>
	<li>Customer can view the total order amount.</li>
	<li>Customer can enter required customer details.</li>
	<li>Customer can place an order.</li>
	<li>System generates a unique Order ID.</li>
	<li>Customer can see the Order ID after successful order placement.</li>
	<li>Customer can contact the store using the provided phone option.</li>
	<li>Store can confirm the order.</li>
	<li>Confirmed orders can be moved to <b>Processing</b> status.</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="3.CustomerJourney"></a>3. Customer Journey</h1>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>HOME
  ↓
VIEW PRODUCTS
  ↓
SEARCH / CATEGORY
  ↓
PRODUCT DETAILS
  ↓
ADD TO CART
  ↓
CART
  ↓
CUSTOMER DETAILS
  ↓
PLACE ORDER
  ↓
ORDER ID CREATED
  ↓
📞 CALL STORE
  ↓
STORE CONFIRMS
  ↓
ORDER PROCESSING</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="4.FunctionalRequirements"></a>4. Functional Requirements</h1>

<h2><a name="FR01%E2%80%93HomePage"></a>FR-01 – Home Page</h2>

<p>The system shall provide a Home page where customers can access the main grocery shopping features.</p>

<h3><a name="Homepageshouldcontain%3A"></a>Home page should contain:</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Store logo/name</li>
	<li>Navigation menu</li>
	<li>Product categories</li>
	<li>Available products</li>
	<li>Search option</li>
	<li>Cart option</li>
	<li>Contact Store option</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<p><b>Given</b> the customer opens Sunil Store<br/>
<b>When</b> the Home page loads<br/>
<b>Then</b> the system should display the available shopping options correctly.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="5.ProductManagement%E2%80%93CustomerSide"></a>5. Product Management – Customer Side</h1>

<h2><a name="FR02%E2%80%93ViewProducts"></a>FR-02 – View Products</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to view available grocery products.</p>

<p>Each product should display:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Product image</li>
	<li>Product name</li>
	<li>Price</li>
	<li>Category</li>
	<li>Availability</li>
	<li>Add to Cart option</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<p><b>Given</b> products are available<br/>
<b>When</b> the customer opens the product section<br/>
<b>Then</b> available products should be displayed with correct information.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR03%E2%80%93SearchProducts"></a>FR-03 – Search Products</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to search for products using product names.</p>

<p>Example:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Customer enters:
"Rice"

↓

System displays:
Rice products</pre>
</div></div>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Search should return matching products.</li>
	<li>Search should not return unrelated products.</li>
	<li>If no product is found, an appropriate message should be displayed.</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="6.CategoryRequirement"></a>6. Category Requirement</h1>

<h2><a name="FR04%E2%80%93BrowsebyCategory"></a>FR-04 – Browse by Category</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to select a category and view products belonging to that category.</p>

<p>Example:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Categories

Rice &amp; Grains
Vegetables
Fruits
Beverages
Snacks
Household
Personal Care</pre>
</div></div>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<p>When the customer selects a category, only relevant products should be displayed.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="7.ProductDetails"></a>7. Product Details</h1>

<h2><a name="FR05%E2%80%93ViewProductDetails"></a>FR-05 – View Product Details</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to open a product and view detailed information.</p>

<h3><a name="Productdetailsshouldinclude%3A"></a>Product details should include:</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Product name</li>
	<li>Product image</li>
	<li>Description</li>
	<li>Price</li>
	<li>Category</li>
	<li>Availability</li>
	<li>Add to Cart button</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="8.ShoppingCart"></a>8. Shopping Cart</h1>

<h2><a name="FR06%E2%80%93AddtoCart"></a>FR-06 – Add to Cart</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to add an available product to the shopping cart.</p>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<p>When the customer clicks <b>Add to Cart</b>, the selected product should appear in the cart.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR07%E2%80%93UpdateQuantity"></a>FR-07 – Update Quantity</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to increase or decrease the quantity of products.</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Rice
Rs. 500

[-]  2  [+]</pre>
</div></div>

<p>The total amount should automatically update.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR08%E2%80%93RemoveProduct"></a>FR-08 – Remove Product</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to remove an item from the cart.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR09%E2%80%93CartSummary"></a>FR-09 – Cart Summary</h2>

<p>The cart should display:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Product name</li>
	<li>Price</li>
	<li>Quantity</li>
	<li>Subtotal</li>
	<li>Total order amount</li>
</ul>


<p>Example:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Rice       Rs.500 × 2 = Rs.1000
Milk       Rs.300 × 1 = Rs.300

Total = Rs.1300</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="9.CustomerDetails"></a>9. Customer Details</h1>

<h2><a name="FR10%E2%80%93EnterCustomerInformation"></a>FR-10 – Enter Customer Information</h2>

<p>Before placing an order, the customer should provide required information.</p>

<h3><a name="Requiredinformation%3A"></a>Required information:</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Customer Name</li>
	<li>Phone Number</li>
	<li>Delivery Address</li>
</ul>


<p>The system should validate required fields.</p>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<p>If required information is missing, the order should not be submitted and the customer should receive an appropriate validation message.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="10.PlaceOrder"></a>10. Place Order</h1>

<h2><a name="FR11%E2%80%93PlaceOrder"></a>FR-11 – Place Order</h2>

<p>Customer should be able to submit the order after reviewing:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Products</li>
	<li>Quantity</li>
	<li>Prices</li>
	<li>Total amount</li>
	<li>Customer information</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="Orderprocess"></a>Order process</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Customer clicks "Place Order"
          ↓
System validates details
          ↓
Order submitted
          ↓
Order saved to database
          ↓
Unique Order ID generated</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="11.OrderID"></a>11. Order ID</h1>

<h2><a name="FR12%E2%80%93GenerateOrderID"></a>FR-12 – Generate Order ID</h2>

<p>After successful order placement, the system should generate a unique Order ID.</p>

<p>Example:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Order Successfully Placed!

Order ID: SUN-000125

Total: Rs. 2,450

Please call Sunil Store to confirm your order.</pre>
</div></div>

<p>The Order ID should be stored together with the order details in the database.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="12.CallStore"></a>12. Call Store</h1>

<h2><a name="FR13%E2%80%93CallStore"></a>FR-13 – Call Store</h2>

<p>After receiving the Order ID, the customer should be able to contact Sunil Store.</p>

<p>A <b>Call Store</b> button can be provided.</p>

<p>On a supported mobile device:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>📞 Call Store
      ↓
Phone dialer opens</pre>
</div></div>

<p>The customer can tell the store:</p>

<blockquote><p>"My Order ID is SUN-000125."</p></blockquote>

<hr />

<h1><a name="13.StoreConfirmation"></a>13. Store Confirmation</h1>

<h2><a name="FR14%E2%80%93ConfirmCustomerOrder"></a>FR-14 – Confirm Customer Order</h2>

<p>After receiving the customer's call, store staff should locate the order using the Order ID.</p>

<p>The admin should be able to verify:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Order ID</li>
	<li>Customer name</li>
	<li>Phone number</li>
	<li>Delivery address</li>
	<li>Products</li>
	<li>Quantities</li>
	<li>Total amount</li>
	<li>Order date/time</li>
</ul>


<p>After confirming the order, the order status should change from:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Pending
   ↓
Confirmed</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="14.OrderProcessing"></a>14. Order Processing</h1>

<h2><a name="FR15%E2%80%93ProcessConfirmedOrder"></a>FR-15 – Process Confirmed Order</h2>

<p>Once the store confirms the order, the order can move to:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Pending
   ↓
Confirmed
   ↓
Processing</pre>
</div></div>

<p>Admin should be able to update the status.</p>

<p>Additional status options can include:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Completed
Cancelled</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="15.AdminPanel"></a>15. Admin Panel</h1>

<h2><a name="FR16%E2%80%93AdminLogin"></a>FR-16 – Admin Login</h2>

<p>Only authorized admin users should be able to access the Admin Panel.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR17%E2%80%93ViewAllOrders"></a>FR-17 – View All Orders</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to view <b>all customer orders</b>.</p>

<p>The order list should display:</p>

<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>Field</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Order ID</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Unique order number</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Customer</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Customer name</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Phone</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Customer phone</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Address</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Delivery address</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Items</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Ordered products</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Quantity</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Product quantity</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Total</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Total order amount</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Date</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Order date/time</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Status</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Current order status</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>


<hr />

<h1><a name="16.AdminOrderManagement"></a>16. Admin Order Management</h1>

<h2><a name="FR18%E2%80%93SearchOrder"></a>FR-18 – Search Order</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to search orders using:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Order ID</li>
	<li>Customer name</li>
	<li>Phone number</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="FR19%E2%80%93UpdateOrderStatus"></a>FR-19 – Update Order Status</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to update order status.</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Pending
   ↓
Confirmed
   ↓
Processing
   ↓
Completed</pre>
</div></div>

<p>Admin should also be able to mark an order as:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Cancelled</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="17.ProductManagement%E2%80%93Admin"></a>17. Product Management – Admin</h1>

<h2><a name="FR20%E2%80%93AddProduct"></a>FR-20 – Add Product</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to add new grocery products.</p>

<p>Required information:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Product name</li>
	<li>Price</li>
	<li>Category</li>
	<li>Image</li>
	<li>Description</li>
	<li>Availability</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="FR21%E2%80%93EditProduct"></a>FR-21 – Edit Product</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to update existing product information.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="FR22%E2%80%93DeleteProduct"></a>FR-22 – Delete Product</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to remove products that are no longer available.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="18.CategoryManagement"></a>18. Category Management</h1>

<h2><a name="FR23%E2%80%93ManageCategories"></a>FR-23 – Manage Categories</h2>

<p>Admin should be able to:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Add category</li>
	<li>Edit category</li>
	<li>Delete category</li>
</ul>


<p>Products should be associated with the correct category.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="19.DatabaseRequirements"></a>19. Database Requirements</h1>

<p>The system should store the following information.</p>

<h3><a name="Product"></a>Product</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Product ID
Product Name
Description
Category
Price
Image
Availability</pre>
</div></div>

<h3><a name="CustomerOrder"></a>Customer Order</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Order ID
Customer Name
Phone Number
Delivery Address
Ordered Products
Quantity
Total Amount
Order Date/Time
Order Status</pre>
</div></div>

<h3><a name="OrderStatus"></a>Order Status</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Pending
Confirmed
Processing
Completed
Cancelled</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<h1><a name="20.APIRequirements"></a>20. API Requirements</h1>

<p>The application should communicate with the database through the existing Vercel API.</p>

<p>Main operations:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>GET    → Products
POST   → Create Order
GET    → Orders
PUT    → Update Order
POST   → Add Product
PUT    → Update Product
DELETE → Delete Product</pre>
</div></div>

<p>The API should return proper success and error responses.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="21.MobileApp%2FPWARequirements"></a>21. Mobile App / PWA Requirements</h1>

<p>The existing website should work as a <b>Progressive Web App (PWA)</b>.</p>

<h3><a name="Customershouldbeableto%3A"></a>Customer should be able to:</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Open Sunil Store
       ↓
Add to Home Screen
       ↓
📱 Sunil Store App</pre>
</div></div>

<p>Play Store upload is <b>not required</b>.</p>

<p>The application should provide:</p>

<ul>
	<li>App icon</li>
	<li>Standalone app mode</li>
	<li>Mobile responsive UI</li>
	<li>PWA manifest</li>
	<li>Service worker</li>
	<li>Mobile-friendly navigation</li>
	<li>Touch-friendly buttons</li>
	<li>Responsive product/cart pages</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="22.SecurityRequirements"></a>22. Security Requirements</h1>

<p>The system should:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Protect Admin Panel</li>
	<li>Validate customer input</li>
	<li>Validate API requests</li>
	<li>Prevent unauthorized admin operations</li>
	<li>Protect database access</li>
	<li>Prevent invalid orders</li>
	<li>Validate product quantities</li>
	<li>Handle invalid requests safely</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="23.NonFunctionalRequirements"></a>23. Non-Functional Requirements</h1>

<h3><a name="Usability"></a>Usability</h3>

<p>The application should be simple and easy to use for normal grocery customers.</p>

<h3><a name="Performance"></a>Performance</h3>

<p>Products and pages should load within a reasonable time.</p>

<h3><a name="Responsiveness"></a>Responsiveness</h3>

<p>The system should work correctly on:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Android phones</li>
	<li>Tablets</li>
	<li>Laptops</li>
	<li>Desktop computers</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="Reliability"></a>Reliability</h3>

<p>Successfully submitted orders should remain stored in the database.</p>

<h3><a name="Availability"></a>Availability</h3>

<p>The application should be accessible through the deployed Vercel environment.</p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="24.MainJiraEpicStructure"></a>24. Main Jira Epic Structure</h1>

<p>ඔයා මේ requirements <b>Jira එකට directly manage කරන්න</b> නම් මේ structure එක use කරන්න:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>EPIC 01 – Customer Shopping

 ├── Story: View Home Page
 ├── Story: View Products
 ├── Story: Search Products
 ├── Story: Browse Products by Category
 └── Story: View Product Details


EPIC 02 – Shopping Cart

 ├── Story: Add Product to Cart
 ├── Story: Update Cart Quantity
 ├── Story: Remove Product from Cart
 └── Story: Calculate Cart Total


EPIC 03 – Customer Order

 ├── Story: Enter Customer Details
 ├── Story: Review Order
 ├── Story: Place Order
 ├── Story: Generate Order ID
 └── Story: Call Store for Order Confirmation


EPIC 04 – Order Management

 ├── Story: Admin View All Orders
 ├── Story: Search Customer Order
 ├── Story: Confirm Order
 ├── Story: Process Order
 ├── Story: Complete Order
 └── Story: Cancel Order


EPIC 05 – Admin Product Management

 ├── Story: Add Product
 ├── Story: Edit Product
 ├── Story: Delete Product
 └── Story: Manage Categories


EPIC 06 – API &amp; Database

 ├── Story: Product API
 ├── Story: Create Order API
 ├── Story: Retrieve Orders
 ├── Story: Update Order Status
 └── Story: Database Validation


EPIC 07 – Mobile PWA

 ├── Story: PWA Manifest
 ├── Story: App Icon
 ├── Story: Service Worker
 ├── Story: Add to Home Screen
 └── Story: Responsive Mobile UI


EPIC 08 – QA Testing

 ├── Functional Testing
 ├── UI Testing
 ├── API Testing
 ├── Database Testing
 ├── Regression Testing
 ├── Performance Testing
 ├── Security Testing
 └── Mobile/PWA Testing</pre>
</div></div>

<h3><a name="%E2%AD%90Mostimportantendtoendrequirement"></a>⭐ Most important end-to-end requirement</h3>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Customer
   ↓
Home
   ↓
Products
   ↓
Search / Category
   ↓
Product Details
   ↓
Add to Cart
   ↓
Cart
   ↓
Customer Details
   ↓
Place Order
   ↓
Order saved in Database
   ↓
Order ID Created
   ↓
📞 Customer Calls Store
   ↓
Admin Finds Order ID
   ↓
Store Confirms Order
   ↓
Confirmed
   ↓
Processing
   ↓
Completed</pre>
</div></div>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

